    "result_text": "Done. The full suite (compiles all of `src/main` plus the one test class) is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe task: on successful owner creation, emit a line via the `NOTIFY` logger containing the owner id and memberId.\n\nRather than pile this onto the existing `OwnerAuditLogger` (which owns the `AUDIT` stream), I gave the new responsibility its own small unit, mirroring the established pattern:\n\n- **`WelcomeNotifier`** (new, `rest/controller/`) \u2014 a `@Component` with a single method `enqueueWelcome(Owner)` that writes one line to a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger carrying `ownerId` and `memberId`. This parallels `OwnerAuditLogger` exactly, keeping notification and audit concerns separate.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 injected the notifier and invoked it in `addOwner(...)` right after the successful save/audit step (`this.welcomeNotifier.enqueueWelcome(owner)`), so it only fires on a successful create.\n\nVerified output during the test run:\n```\nINFO  NOTIFY - Welcome notification queued: ownerId=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n```\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
